  "Comments": "Isoamyl alcohol, the main compound of the fusel oil of cane distilleries. Critical point 579.4 K, 39.3 bar (NIST Chemistry WebBook: Majer and Svoboda 1985; Gude and Teja 1995), normal boiling point 404.2 K. Vapor pressure: the DIPPR 101 equation of the isomer 2-methyl-1-butanol (ChemSep) taken by corresponding states to this critical point and shifted to the boiling point; it gives the enthalpy of vaporization of Majer and Svoboda within 2 % from 303 to 395 K. Liquid density of the isomer scaled to 810 kg/m3 at 20 C. Ideal gas formation enthalpy -300.8 kJ/mol (liquid -356.4 kJ/mol plus 55.6 kJ/mol of vaporization at 25 C). Heat capacities, transport properties and UNIFAC groups are those of the isomer (the same groups), in the units of ChemSep except the liquid density, in kg/m3 as the user database reads it.",
